; Total Commander JAWS scripts: key assignments
; Copyright (c) 2026 author. MIT License.
; Alt+digit (columns) and Alt+Shift+letter families: free in Total Commander 11.56 and in
; JAWS 2025 defaults (Alt+8/9 only in the Classic Laptop layout).
; Subject to change (decision 2026-11-17).

[Common Keys]
Alt+1=TcSayColumn1
Alt+2=TcSayColumn2
Alt+3=TcSayColumn3
Alt+4=TcSayColumn4
Alt+5=TcSayColumn5
Alt+6=TcSayColumn6
Alt+7=TcSayColumn7
Alt+8=TcSayColumn8
Alt+9=TcSayColumn9
Alt+Shift+P=TcSayPath
Alt+Shift+A=TcSayActivePanel
; Lister font size, Ctrl+0: back to the stored size, with a sound (decision 2026-11-20).
; The main keyboard "+" and "-" are not assigned here, so they keep their key echo; the
; scripts follow them in KeyPressedEvent.
Control+0=TcListerZoomReset
; Insert keys (decision 2026-11-25): which Insert marks is set in Quick Settings (Selection key,
; Usage) and applied while Total Commander has the focus; a line for a key that is a JAWS key
; is not used while JAWSKey has a line of its own: without it, the JAWS key pressed alone
; ran the Insert line (measured 2026-11-25). The JAWS key alone does nothing, also twice.
; JAWS's key names (Default.JKM modifiers): ExtInsert, NumInsert, and Insert for either.
; The numeric Insert as a plain key is NumInsert; with only the Insert line it went to TC
; without the script (measured 2026-11-25).
ExtInsert=TcInsertMark
NumInsert=TcInsertMark
Insert=TcInsertMark
JAWSKey=TcJawsKeyTwice
